  "description": "AXUJAF crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C128 H194 Cl10 Cu8 Dy4 N8 O29 2+,2(Cl1 1-),8(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 2 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 2 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1B (Cu) has 2 O neighbors; Cu2B (Cu) has 2 O neighbors; Cu3B (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Cu4B (Cu) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 26 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.293-5.674 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.44-174.21°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4Cu8L8(μ2-H2O)(μ3-OH)8Cl10(H2O)4]Cl2·6MeCN (HL = 5,7-di-tert-butyl-2-methylenehydroxylbenzoxazole). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
